From c51659551c1ef14a09a03eebe0ba45acdf6d88a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:28:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban capability owner: generation-aware rejection
 wake text; overlap docstring/comments (PR #2231 review nits)

Follow-up to #2231 (review 5891577400, card t_01a1d50b5110a4b1).

1. wait_check's rejection text (_rejected) always promised "Blocking again with the same needs routes one
   fresh request (a new generation)", but _route_generations grants a fresh generation only to a
   generation-1 request that was rejected or expired. A generation-2 refusal or any failed request is
   refused capability_route_exhausted, so a woken card followed the text into a dead end. The text now reads
   the generation from the request id (::g<N>) and the state: it promises generation 2 only where routing
   grants it, and otherwise says the route is exhausted and what to do instead (continue/link the card that
   owns the work, fix the named cause, or a needs_input human_request when only David can clear it). The
   "was expired/failed by <gw>" wording is now "expired before <gw> answered it" / "failed on <gw>", and a
   refusal ending in "." no longer prints "..".
   Test: test_wake_text_promises_a_fresh_request_only_when_routing_grants_one checks gen-1 rejected,
   gen-1 expired, gen-2 rejected and failed against what _route_generations actually does next
   (RED on main: the gen-2/failed text promises a fresh request).
2. kanban_overlap module docstring: singletons also honour the _bound_to exemption, not only the waiting card.
3. Comments: _bound_to / bound_cards match awaiting.ref by bare id, ignoring awaiting.gateway (relies on
   globally unique task ids); _PLACED_FROM trusts any body line in the forward-footer shape, acceptable for a
   heuristic overlap exemption limited to the card's own capability-owner create.

Proof: hermes-core-wt test over the 14 files importing kanban_capability_routing / kanban_overlap:
620 passed, 0 failed. scripts/check --base origin/main: 19 checks ok.
